      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is unsafe as written.\n\n- **Daily total:** 2000 mg three times daily comes to 6,000 mg/day. The usual adult maximum is 4,000 mg/day, and many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day. At 6 g/day there is a real risk of hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n- **Single dose:** 2000 mg is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 1,000 mg.\n\nTypical options for a 70 kg adult with normal liver and kidney function are:\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg PO every 8 hours** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg PO every 6 hours** (4,000 mg/day), which is the ceiling\n\nTell me which regimen you want, or confirm the intended dose if I've misread it. Please also check with your resident or the supervising physician. I'll enter the order as soon as you confirm."
